# {{ component.name }}

A general Rust package with both a library and executable entrypoint. Single-project and monorepo `apps`/`packages`
placements use the same sources; placement does not select another runtime or crate structure.
There are no product features, external dependencies, Tokio, FFI or CLI parsers yet.

## Code and responsibilities

- `src/lib.rs`: public boundary for reusable types/functions; currently crate documentation only, with no product API.
- `src/main.rs`: executable entrypoint; `main()` currently exits without I/O. Add argument/configuration composition and
  error/exit-code translation here; place behavior needed by other callers in the library.
- `tests/`: future public-boundary integration tests; there are currently **zero product tests**.
- `Cargo.toml`: package, edition and dependencies; Cargo conventions discover both targets.

Expose only the required `pub`/`pub(crate)` surface. Return meaningful `Result` values for expected failures rather than
panicking. Make mutable-state and resource lifetimes explicit through ownership/borrowing. Do not pre-create traits,
repositories, domain layers or tasks without an actual substitution/test boundary.
Additional executables belong in the package's `src/bin/`; repository-root `bin/` is not a Cargo target directory.

## Environment and checks

Use a compiler supporting Rust 2021, with rustfmt and Clippy. Development toolchain pins and supported MSRV are separate
contracts; choosing an edition does not validate a minimum compiler. This package owns its Cargo environment and lock.
Review and retain `Cargo.lock` because the package includes an executable. If adopting a parent Cargo workspace, define
membership and shared lock/toolchain ownership together. Python/JavaScript checks do not replace Cargo checks.

The scaffold has no external dependencies, so native checks/builds can run offline. Revisit installation, lock updates
and environment-specific commands when adding dependencies.

```sh
cargo fmt --check
cargo clippy --offline --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test --offline
cargo build --offline --lib --bin {{ component.name }}
cargo run --offline --quiet --bin {{ component.name }}
```

The current harness has zero product tests and the executable does nothing. Successful commands establish native
scaffold compilation/loading, not business behavior, external compatibility, deployment or physical operation.

